<Base
  title="About — Terrence Breschi"
  description="Terrence Breschi. I lead strategy, build prototypes, ship code, and teach others."
  section="about"
>
  <div class="entry-header">
    <h2>Hey there, I'm Terrence.</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lede">
      I'm the Principal Product Designer for AI at Personio. I lead strategy, build
      prototypes, ship code, and teach others.
    </p>

    <p>
      It's an exciting time to be creative. The gaps between understanding problems,
      designing solutions, building products, and communicating value are rapidly
      shrinking.
    </p>

    <p>
      I'd call myself an <strong>optimistic accelerationist</strong>—I'm genuinely
      excited about integrating AI into each step of my process. I learn, plan, and
      prototype with AI. I build my own tools and ship production code with AI. I'm
      even maintaining open source software these days.
    </p>

    <p>
      At Personio, I'm building AI that's evolving the HR landscape. At Meta, I led
      design on products used by millions of people. At Classy I launched a platform
      that raised billions for nonprofits. Along the way I've worked with incredible
      people who taught me how to think and act intentionally.
    </p>

    <p>
      What motivates me is <strong>clarity of thought and action</strong>. Recognizing
      a problem, building a solution, and sharing it with others.
    </p>

    <p><strong>I move fast and learn things.</strong></p>

    <p>
      What I'm looking for right now are AI-first projects with AI-native teams—people
      who are excited about the technology and committed to doing it safely.
    </p>

    <p>If that sounds like you, or someone you know, I'd love to talk.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="subscribe">
    <p>New York.</p>
    <div class="link-container">
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/tbreschi/" class="project-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">linkedin</a>
      <a href="mailto:t@bresch.io" class="project-link">t@bresch.io</a>
    </div>
  </div>
